{
  "comment": "Decoding of a stored cell is exact: a cell decodes only in the form the encoder writes, and anything else is CODEC_DECODE (docs/codec.md, Decoding is exact). A case gives the stage list in write order, the stored cell as text (stored) or as the hex of its bytes (stored_hex), and the decoded value or the error code. A list of host stages without aes (hex, ip) decodes with the host decode of the client and no key; any other list decodes with the codec decode. Base64 is the padded standard alphabet with zero padding bits, without white space or line breaks; hex accepts both letter cases, as MySQL UNHEX does on the SQL side of the same stage.",
